Subject: Object creation: learned instance capacity (slack tracking)

What this does
  Object creation: learned instance capacity (slack tracking).

Why we need it
  And the shape's `prop_size` doubles on growth, so the ProseMirror `Node` and `TextNode` both grow out of the 2-slot inline property array on every construction.

What it adds
  `JS_CallConstructorInternal`'s legacy branch asks `js_new_target_bytecode` for the `new.target`'s `JSFunctionBytecode` and passes its `inst_inline_cap` to `js_create_from_ctor_cap` -> `JS_NewObjectProtoClassCap` -> `JS_NewObjectFromShapeCap`, which reserves that many inline property slots for `JS_CLASS_OBJECT`; after the constructor returns `js_learn_instance_cap` records the largest instance `shape->prop_size` seen, and after `JS_OBJ_LEARN_SAMPLES` constructions the constructor publishes `inst_inline_cap = max(seen)` capped at `JS_OBJ_LEARNED_INLINE_MAX`. Keying on `new.target` lets a base constructor learn the subclass layout.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
